inst any real-world source**.\n\n---\n\n## What You Should Do\n\n1. **Check where you encountered this citation.** Was it suggested by an AI chatbot, a course reading list, or another source? If an AI tool provided it, that is the likely origin of the fabrication.\n2. **Verify citations before building seminar work around them.** Use WorldCat (worldcat.org), Google Scholar, or your library's catalog to confirm a book exists before using it.\n3. **For your actual seminar needs**, I can help you find *real* scholarly work on silence and non-verbal communication in Pacific societies. This is a genuine and rich area of study, with real scholars such as:\n   - **Keith Basso** (silence in cross-cultural communication)\n   - **Adam Kendon** (gesture and non-verbal communication)\n   - Work in journals like *Oceania*, *Journal of the Polynesian Society*, and *Language in Society*\n\nWould you like me to find verified, real sources on this topic for your linguistic anthropology seminar?",
